msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1045 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1238
msgid "Round to nearest, with ties to even"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1046 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1234
msgid "`rz`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1047 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1235
msgid "Round towards zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1048 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1240
msgid "`rp`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1049 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1241
msgid "Round towards positive infinity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1050
msgid "`rs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1051
msgid ""
"Stochastic rounding which is achieved through the use of the supplied random "
"bits (`%rnd_bits`). The result s rounded in the direction towards zero or "
"away from zero based on the carry out of the integer addition of the of "
"mantissa from the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1059
msgid ""
"Some conversions involve a scale factor of type `ue8m0`. For `scale.n2."
"ue8m0`, the operand is a packed 16-bit integer containing two `ue8m0` scale "
"values, one for each input. For `scale.n1.ue8m0`, a single `ue8m0` scale "
"factor is applied to both inputs. For down conversion, inputs are divided by "
"`scale_factor` and then the conversion is performed. For up-conversion,  "
"inputs are converted to destination type and then multiplied by "
"`scale_factor`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1066
msgid "`fp8` Conversion Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1093
msgid ""
"These intrinsics perform conversions involving the `e4m3`, `e5m2`, `ue8m0`, "
"and `ue5m3` narrow floating-point formats. In case of two inputs, the value "
"converted from input `%a` is stored in the upper 8-bits of the result, and "
"the value converted from input `%b` is stored in the lower 8-bits of the "
"result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1099 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1133
#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1168 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1204
msgid "For rounding modes, see {ref}`narrow-fp-rounding-modes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1101 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1135
#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1170 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1206
msgid "The `relu` modifier clamps negative results to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1103
msgid ""
"When `satfinite` is specified, if the absolute value of input (ignoring "
"sign) is greater than `MAX_NORM` of the specified destination format, then "
"the result is sign-preserved `MAX_NORM` of the destination format and a "
"positive `MAX_NORM` in `.ue8m0x2`/`.ue5m3x2` for which the destination sign "
"is not supported. Also, if the input value is `NaN`, then the result is "
"`NaN` in the specified destination format. The `satfinite` modifier is "
"assumed to be present for conversions involving `e4m3` and `e5m2` types as "
"the destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1112 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1143
#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1178 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1214
msgid "For scale factor, see {ref}`scale-factor <scale-factor>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1114 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1145
#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1180 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1216
msgid ""
"For more information, see [PTX ISA](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/parallel-"
"thread-execution/#data-movement-and-conversion-instructions-cvt)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1116
msgid "`s2f6` Conversion Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1128
msgid ""
"These intrinsics perform conversions involving the `s2f6` narrow floating-"
"point format. In case of two inputs, the value converted from input `%a` is "
"stored in the upper 8-bits of the result, and the value converted from input "
"`%b` is stored in the lower 8-bits of the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1137 ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1172
#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1208
msgid ""
"When `satfinite` is specified, if the absolute value of input (ignoring "
"sign) is greater than `MAX_NORM` of the specified destination format, then "
"the result is sign-preserved `MAX_NORM` of the destination format. Also, if "
"the input is `NaN`, then the result is the positive `MAX_NORM` of the "
"destination format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1147
msgid "`fp6` Conversion Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1162
msgid ""
"These intrinsics perform conversions involving the `e2m3` and `e3m2` narrow "
"floating-point formats. In case of two inputs, the value converted from "
"input `%a` is stored in the upper 8-bits of the result, and the value "
"converted from input `%b` is stored in the lower 8-bits of the result with 2 "
"MSBs padded with 0s in both cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1182
msgid "`fp4` Conversion Intrinsics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../NVPTXUsage.md:1197
msgid ""
"These intrinsics perform conversions involving the `e2m1` narrow floating-"
"point format. For conversions involving `e2m1x2`, the packed `e2m1x2` value "
"is stored in the lower byte of the `i16` argument or result. In case of two "
"inputs, the value converted from input `%a` is stored in the upper 4-bits of "
"the result, and the value converted from input `%b` is stored in the lower 4-"
"bits of the result."
msgstr ""

